Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 18:22:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 029/143] dts: opi4a: PD_VO0 on tcon-top/tcon-tv and CLK_DE at
 600MHz like the BSP

Audit findings vs BSP: the series dtsi does not claim the VO0 island from
tcon-top/tcon-tv (only from hdmi) and does not pin the rate/parent of CLK_DE
(the BSP uses PLL_VIDEO3_4X @600MHz via assigned-clocks).
---
 .../dts/allwinner/sun55i-t527-orangepi-4a.dts | 24 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-t527-orangepi-4a.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-t527-orangepi-4a.dts
index ca2e27825..c874851cb 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-t527-orangepi-4a.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-t527-orangepi-4a.dts
@@ -630,3 +630,27 @@ hdmi_out_con: endpoint {
 		remote-endpoint = <&hdmi_con_in>;
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * Changes from the audit against the 5.15 BSP:
+ * - The BSP hangs vo0/tcon off the VO0 island (A523_PCK_VO0); the patch's
+ *   dtsi only claims it from the hdmi node. Claiming it also in
+ *   tcon-top and tcon-tv avoids touching registers with the island off and
+ *   protects against the sync_state sweep (it already bit with simpledrm).
+ * - The BSP sets CLK_DE to 600 MHz under PLL_VIDEO3_4X
+ *   (assigned-clocks of the BSP's de@5000000 node); the patch's dtsi
+ *   set no rate and the mux could stay on the reset parent.
+ */
+&tcon_top {
+	power-domains = <&pck600 PD_VO0>;
+};
+
+&tcon_tv0 {
+	power-domains = <&pck600 PD_VO0>;
+};
+
+&display_clocks {
+	assigned-clocks = <&ccu CLK_DE>;
+	assigned-clock-parents = <&ccu CLK_PLL_VIDEO3_4X>;
+	assigned-clock-rates = <600000000>;
+};
